    <namerecord nameID="9" platformID="0" platEncID="0" langID="0x0">
      Christian Munk
    </namerecord>
    <namerecord nameID="10" platformID="0" platEncID="0" langID="0x0">
      “Metro Sans” was built with FontStruct
Designer description: I made this, because I was bothered with the quality of the font used on the displays of the Copenhagen Metro. So this is an attempt to make a better font under the same restrictions (i.e. a display with a height of 14 LED lamps). The o - and possibly other characters - are the same as in the current font. But I made sure the M became similar to the logo of the metro. Don't mind the IPA, I just went a bit wild...

    </namerecord>
    <namerecord nameID="11" platformID="0" platEncID="0" langID="0x0">
      https://fontstruct.com/fontstructions/show/723864/metro_sans
    </namerecord>
    <namerecord nameID="12" platformID="0" platEncID="0" langID="0x0">
      https://fontstruct.com/fontstructors/show/25776/cmunk
    </namerecord>
    <namerecord nameID="13" platformID="0" platEncID="0" langID="0x0">
      Creative Commons Attribution Share Alike
    </namerecord>
    <namerecord nameID="14" platformID="0" platEncID="0" langID="0x0">
      http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/
    </namerecord>
    <namerecord nameID="19" platformID="0" platEncID="0" langID="0x0">
      Five big quacking zephyrs jolt my wax bed
    </namerecord>
    <namerecord nameID="256" platformID="0" platEncID="0" langID="0x0">
      BQsLfV9g
    </namerecord>
